, "title_zh": "急診科創傷患者CT檢查中需要介入之附帶發現的盛行率：系統性回顧與統合分析", "source": "PubMed", "journal": "BMJ open", "year": 2026, "doi": "10.1001/jama.2022.21383", "design": "systematic_review_meta", "design_label": "系統性回顧/統合", "design_evidence": "Systematic review and meta-analysis. PubMed, EMBASE and Cochrane CENTRAL databases from database inception to 22 November 2024. Bayesian multivariate random-effects meta-analysis of prevalence.", "topics": ["創傷"], "methods": ["meta_analysis_pooled"], "sample_size": 18538, "age_group": "adult", "setting": "emergency department", "country": "mainly high-income countries", "primary_outcome": "需要任何介入之偶發發現的盛行率及需要緊急介入之子集的盛行率", "effect_size": "IFs requiring any interventions 29.8% (95% CrI 20.4–42.9%); urgent interventions 7.6% (95% CrI 4.5–14.8%); pathologically confirmed cancers 0.6% (95% CrI 0.3–1.6%); emergent non-traumatic vascular pathologies 0.3% (95% CrI 0.1–0.9%)", "key_findings": ["Whole-body CT: 29.8% IFs requiring any intervention, 7.6% requiring urgent intervention", "Pathologically confirmed cancers 0.6%, emergent vascular pathologies 0.3%", "Detection frequency reduced with narrowed scanned body regions; sparse head/neck/spine data"], "limitations": {"selection_bias": "22 項研究主要來自高收入國家；21 項回溯性設計；基於臨床實踐的有限品質資料", "confounding": "IF 分級標準不統一；影像判讀者的經驗和專業知識多樣化", "missing_data": "頭部、頸部和脊柱資料稀少導致結果有限", "other": "放射科醫師建議和臨床實踐中的報告變異；缺乏標準化分類和報告系統"}, "quality": 4, "quality_rationale": "高品質 PRISMA 系統性回顧，雙重篩選、雙重評估、雙重資料萃取、Bayesian 統合分析與 GRADE 確定性分級；受限於異質原始研究與非一致分級標準", "rel_clinical": 2, "rel_education": 0, "scope_note": "Systematic review of trauma CT findings in ED; incidental findings are detected during trauma imaging but management decisions are primarily hospital-based radiology/oncology domain, not院前 decision-making. Relevance to院前 is indirect (epidemiology of what gets found) rather than direct (院前 personnel do not perform CT or manage these findings). Educational value minimal as review focuses on prevalence, not training/skill.", "review": 0